{"id": "unknown-2026-07-22-008", "date": "2026-07-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Weekly price shock alert: Polyester feedstock - week ended July 17", "content": "MEG CFR Southeast Asia surged 25.93 per cent in the week to July 20 as Hormuz-linked disruptions tightened Gulf cargoes to Asia.\nPX and PTA also rose, but weak downstream textile demand limited polyester yarn price pass-through and squeezed mill margins.\nChina’s coal-based MEG capacity cushioned supply, while India’s PTA and MEG duty expiry added import-cost pressure for producers.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/weekly-price-shock-alert-polyester-feedstock-week-ended-july-17-311958-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-22-009", "date": "2026-07-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Weekly price shock alert: Regenerated (MMCF) - week ended July 17", "content": "Pakistan's Modal 1.4D price rose 4.10 per cent in the week ended July 17, driven by energy and raw-material costs rather than currency weakness.\nIndia's Liva Eco yarn gained 3.33 to 3.70 per cent, while Ecovero, Tencel and Modal yarn quotes stayed unchanged.\nStable China prices and lower VSF inventories point to supply discipline, shaping sourcing risk for spinners and buyers.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/weekly-price-shock-alert-regenerated-mmcf-week-ended-july-17-311953-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-22-010", "date": "2026-07-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India's DGFT proposes RCMC exemption for small export consignments", "content": "India's DGFT has proposed exempting export consignments with an FOB value of up to ₹10,000 from the requirement to obtain an RCMC under the Foreign Trade Policy 2023.\nIt aims to promote small-value exports through postal and courier channels by reducing compliance costs for MSMEs, artisans and D2C brands.\nIt will not apply to restricted goods, and stakeholders have been invited to submit comments.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-dgft-proposes-rcmc-exemption-for-small-export-consignments-311961-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-22-011", "date": "2026-07-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.25, "keywords": ["record", "[否定]growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "British International Investment unveils 2026-2031 Bangladesh strategy", "content": "British International Investment (BII) has launched its 2026-2031 strategy in Bangladesh, reaffirming its long-term commitment to supporting sustainable and inclusive economic growth in the country. \nThe strategy will build on its past track record by partnering with businesses to create more jobs, strengthen economic resilience, advance gender inclusion and support transition to a greener economy. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/british-international-investment-unveils-2026-2031-bangladesh-strategy-311954-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-22-012", "date": "2026-07-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["delay"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ICE cotton extends gains for second day on higher crude oil", "content": "ICE cotton futures extended gains for a second consecutive session, with the December 2026 contract settling 1.90 per cent higher at 80.42 cents per pound.\nStronger crude oil prices, successful Chinese state cotton reserve auctions and delayed cotton planting in India supported prices.\nHowever, the rally came on the lightest trading volume of 2026, indicating mainly short covering.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-extends-gains-for-second-day-on-higher-crude-oil-311956-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-22-013", "date": "2026-07-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Trident's ₹100 cr innovation push redefines home textiles", "content": "Trident invested ₹100+ crore (~$12 million+) in R&D, backed by 17+ patents and 147 trademarks, strengthening India's home-textile innovation.\nFY26 EBITDA margins ranged from 9.1 per cent (Welspun) to 21.1 per cent (Himatsingka), highlighting profitability as a key differentiator.\nLower US tariffs and duty-free access to the EU and UK improve FY27 export prospects.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/trident-s-100-cr-innovation-push-redefines-home-textiles-311945-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-22-014", "date": "2026-07-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Weekly price shock alert: PFY (DTY & POY) - week ended July 17", "content": "India's DTY rose 3.15 per cent, outpacing China's 1.38 per cent gain as rupee weakness and QCO enforcement enabled full cost pass-through, while Pakistan stayed flat. \nIndia and China reached rare DTY price parity at ~$1.36/kg despite contrasting domestic market dynamics. \nCrude surged 12–14 per cent, but weak textile demand and lower MEG prices limited cost pass-through across Asia's polyester chain.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/weekly-price-shock-alert-pfy-dty-poy-week-ended-july-17-311936-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-22-015", "date": "2026-07-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "UV-resistant and fan-powered: India's next performance fabric frontier", "content": "Zeel Climate Clothing has shown summer apparel prototypes at Bharat Tex 2026 using UV-resistant, heat-resistant and moisture-absorbent synthetic fabric with fan-assisted air circulation.\nThe India-focused launch signals growing demand for functional fashion as heatwaves reshape clothing needs.\nZeel is selling direct-to-consumer first, with scale-up planned after consumer response data.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/uv-resistant-and-fan-powered-india-s-next-performance-fabric-frontier-311947-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
